  "narrative": {
    "text": "**Business & market dynamics:** Demand visibly re-accelerated in the core retail channel, with comparable sales growing as the company recaptured both new and returning customers across residential and professional segments. Customer re-engagement efforts gained traction, lifting store-level productivity. The seasonal quarter’s top-line outcome surprised to the upside, while margin expansion reflected better volume absorption and improved pricing. Broader macro or competitive headwinds were absent from the commentary; instead, the narrative centered on organic demand healing and a strengthening sell-through environment in the aftermarket pool space.\n\n**Management strategy and execution:** Leadership emphasized disciplined cost control, strategic pricing, and focused customer re-engagement as the engines behind the margin recovery. The team delivered full-year revenue guidance above consensus, signaling confidence in the trajectory. Though a non-GAAP loss missed headline estimates, the operational beat and forward outlook dominated the reaction, rewarding management’s credibility after prior turbulence. The decisive stock surge suggests the market now views execution as back on track and the multi-quarter turnaround gaining legitimacy.",
